#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Questions e responsas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I cannot see my house on the map / Why should I use &marble; if there is "
"Google Earth already?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&marble; aims to be a lightweight fast educational geographical browser that "
"easily runs on any plattform that is supported by &Qt;. While higher "
"resolution maps would be nice to have they aren't necessary for every user "
"and every use case (just like you don't use a full blown text processor each "
"time you just need a simple editor). Also notice &marble; is free software "
"and is based on data that can be freely redistributed in the same way that "
"applies to Free Software."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why is &marble; so fast although I don't have hardware acceleration "
"enabled? /"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why doesn't &marble; run smoothly on my expensive 3D graphics card?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Despite depicting the earth as a globe &marble; doesn't make use of any 3D "
"hardware acceleration. This has got the advantage that it basically runs at "
"decent speed on any plattform and hardware supported by &Qt;. However it has "
"the disadvantage that it doesn't run as smooth as it could if it used "
"hardware accelerated OpenGL. &marble; just uses plain 2D graphics and "
"therefore requires a graphics adapter that is fast at drawing 2D graphics. "
"We plan to add an optional OpenGL backend in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Will I ever have to pay for &marble;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No, never. But the authors always welcome feedback. &marble; is licensed "
"under the <ulink url=\"http://www.gnu.org/licenses/licenses.html#LGPL"
"\">LGPL</ulink>, so you will never have to pay for this program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I contribute?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&marble; is not only an application but also a Free Software project. As "
"such it's easy to join: just contact us via the kde-edu mailing list (kde-"
"edu@kde.org)."
msgstr ""

